/target
Cargo.lock
.bulba/
__pycache__/

# NOT `*.py` / `*.bin`. Those were inherited from a standalone-repo template
# and they excluded exactly the two things this crate's bit-exactness test
# loads: the reference generator and the fixtures it produces. A .gitignore
# that makes a test's oracle uncommittable is a false claim about the test.
#
# These negations must stay LAST and must name the two paths. `gitignore`
# precedence is deepest-file-wins, so these also override the `**/*.bin` in
# ../../../.gitignore and the `*.bin` in the dormouse root; `git check-ignore
# -v tests/ref_data/tiny.bin` must report THIS file, not a parent.
#
# Plainly, as of 2026-09-27: **neither file exists yet.** The narrow patterns
# above only make them committable. `tests/cmp_reference.rs` is still
# unrunnable — no `gen_reference.py`, no `tests/ref_data/*.bin`, and the
# `binary-tests` feature is still not in `default`. Reference data must come
# from a run of EctoSpace/SCT `spectral_compact_training/spectral_layer.py`;
# it must not be hand-written to make the test pass. See ADR-0020 item 1.
!tests/gen_reference.py
!tests/ref_data/*.bin
